---
description: Fail-closed editorial and Builder CMS controls for blog publishing workflow artifacts.
globs: .builder/skills/blog-publishing/**, docs/skills/blog-publishing.md, scripts/blog/**, content/blog/**, app/blog/**, app/preview/page.tsx, app/llms.txt/**, app/api/blog-markdown/**, components/blog/**, lib/blog/**, lib/builder/client.ts, types/blog.types.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

- Load the `blog-publishing` skill and treat `docs/skills/blog-publishing.md` as authoritative.
- A short blog-creation prompt activates the complete workflow. Load policy/taxonomy/assets, derive safe defaults, check duplicate intent, and default to English draft; never infer publish authorization or asset approval.
- Validate structured inputs with `scripts/blog/validate-blog.ts` before any Builder CMS write.
- Create or revise a draft first. Publishing, scheduling, updating, and archiving require an explicit requested action and a passing result.
- Use approved brand voice/taxonomy values and relevant approved Builder Media assets with complete rights and alt metadata. No suitable approved image means the post remains draft.
- Match the long-form quality bar with useful framing, source-backed analysis, scannable H2/H3 sections, tradeoffs, decision guidance, visible sources, and non-repetitive FAQs where relevant; do not pad or invent evidence.
- Keep claims traceable to primary-source citation-ledger records. Do not invent sources, quotes, rights, approvals, or dates.
- The article shell owns the only H1; Builder body headings start at H2. Preserve visible FAQ, citation, image, author-type, taxonomy, date, and reading-time fields used by Schema.org output.
- Preview the exact saved draft and verify imagery, responsive readability, blocks, links, citations, CTA, navigation, and that Builder bootstrap JavaScript is not visible as content.
- Keep HTML canonical. Generate `/blog/{slug}.md` and `/llms.txt` from public normalized Builder data; exclude drafts/no-index entries from discovery and never maintain duplicate copy.
- Fail closed on legal, copyright/originality, rights, secret, and authorization failures; legal failures cannot be overridden.
- Allow only authorized, auditable non-legal overrides enumerated by the validator.
- Never store secrets, credentials, personal data, chain-of-thought, or hidden reasoning in content or audit records.
